  "task_id": "tmm_optimize_a_22_layer_planar_multilayer_filter_on__7beb390651",
  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer planar multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate with alternating ZnS (high index) and MgF2 (low index) layers under normal unpolarized illumination. Initialize all 22 layer thicknesses to quarter-wave optical thickness at 3300 nm center wavelength (ZnS: n*thickness = 3300/4 nm, MgF2: n*thickness = 3300/4 nm using material refractive indices). Constrain all thicknesses to [50, 950] nm bounds. Use gradient-based thickness optimization to maximize mean transmittance in passbands (3250-3350 nm and 4200-4300 nm) while minimizing mean transmittance in stopbands (2500-3100 nm and 4450-5000 nm). Evaluate using coherent transfer matrix method across 2500-5000 nm wavelength range. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
